    "name": "get_spatial_map",
    "description": "Read ActiveVision 30cm grid in base_link: X [0,.6), Y [-.6,.6), Z [0,.6). 16 cells, stable IDs, ROS last_scanned time (zero=never), latest observed cell IDs and camera pose/forward/up. Sampled valid depth rays mark traversed empty and hit cells, not cells behind hits. >=3 rays qualify; not full-cell coverage or collision clearance. header is last observation time, not query time.  Read-only, final service response/snapshot, never an asynchronous start acknowledgment. No prerequisites except an available ROS service; missing session/context is a backend failure. No supplied task/object/attempt identity is inferred. Inspect raw response and its status; running/cancelled queue states remain inside state_json/results, not fabricated from transport success. 5 second timeout; timeout/cancellation/disconnect does not cancel ROS work and gives no robot-stop guarantee. Read retries are allowed and yield a new snapshot; there is no actuator retry. Next: inspect related state/resources and tool availability. ROS strings/enums remain exact; timestamps use ROS sec/nanosec; revisions are unsigned integers. No default coordinate frame overrides message headers.",
